# Amanah UI design

When adding or changing UI, follow `docs/design-guidelines.md`. In short:

- One product: the public site and the staff workspace share tokens (`src/app/globals.css`) and controls (`src/components/ui.tsx`, `site-header.tsx`). Keep the exact palette, the keyhole mark and the AMANAH | أمانة wordmark.
- Shapes come from a lost-property desk: tag (`.shape-tag`, on an aria-hidden layer behind the content), torn slip (`.edge-torn`), perforation (`.perforation`). Use them as fills, sparingly, never on real report data in public views.
- Cormorant for headings and item names, DM Sans for body text and every number, Amiri for Arabic (`lang="ar" dir="rtl"`). No uppercase eyebrow labels and no 01/02 numbering.
- Pill buttons at least 44px tall that may wrap and never exceed their container; 48px fields with a forest focus ring. Don't stack conflicting Tailwind utilities.
- Surfaces separate by tone, not shadow. Green means approved, red (`destructive`, `bad-*`) means rejected.
- Phone first. Narrow panels use container queries (`@container`, `@md:`). Nothing may extend past a 390px viewport.
- Motion is small and once, and it is removed under reduced motion. Every screen has loading, empty, error and success states.
- Describe only real capabilities. Staff decide every claim.
